# The script the gate has an editor's headless mode run for the package
# `shipped-themes` (tools/package-set.sh run), against the config in
# `config/`, which defines two themes, `first` and `second`,
# and names `first`, then switches to `second` and to two shipped themes.
# What it prints must be exactly `expected`.

reload
settle

# A key makes the frame, and its scene is drawn in `first`, the theme the
# config names: the scene line ends with the theme's name.
key <Escape> Escape -
scene

# `load-theme` asks for a theme's name, with the registered themes as its
# candidates. `second` is typed and accepted: the theme is switched with no
# reload, and the scene after it is drawn in `second`. The switch publishes
# a scene of its own, after the accept's.
run load-theme
commit second
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# A shipped theme is loaded the same way: `solarized-dark`, which this
# package registers (`ShippedThemes.package`), and the scene after it is
# drawn in it.
run load-theme
commit solarized-dark
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# And so is `fairy-floss`, shipped beside it: the scene after it is drawn in
# `fairy-floss`.
run load-theme
commit fairy-floss
key <Enter> Enter -
scene
